Third-party components
----------------------

Trustless Work single-release escrow (v1)
  Source: https://github.com/Trustless-Work/trustlesswork-smart-contract-stellar
  This repository does NOT vendor or redistribute Trustless Work source code or
  compiled Wasm. contracts/third_party/tw-wasm/fetch.sh downloads the escrow Wasm
  that Trustless Work has deployed on Stellar testnet and mainnet, identified by
  its SHA-256 hash, and checks it against contracts/third_party/tw-wasm/SHA256SUMS.
  The downloaded files are git-ignored and used only by the guard contract tests.
  Trustless Work code remains under its own license and copyright.

  The guard contract contains a minimal Rust mirror of the public v1 escrow
  storage types (Escrow, Roles, Milestone, Flags, Trustline) so that it can decode
  `get_escrow`. Those type definitions describe Trustless Work's on-chain data
  layout; see the source repository above for the original.

Circle EURC, Bridge, Privy and Stellar Wallets Kit
  Referenced by public identifiers (asset codes, contract IDs, API names) only.
  No code from these projects is included. All trademarks belong to their owners.

Stellar SDKs
  @stellar/stellar-sdk (Apache-2.0) and soroban-sdk (Apache-2.0) are dependencies,
  installed by npm and cargo, not vendored.
